07:06.960 --> 07:14.080
we're proposing greater flexibility for how the national tariff operates to support new payment models that aid

07:14.080 --> 07:21.680
care integration we're proposing to remove the 2012 act repeal of the ability of the secretary of state

07:21.680 --> 07:28.880
to create NHS trusts this is to make it easier to help systems such as for example dudley who have been developing

07:29.520 --> 07:35.840
what they call their mcp model to create a statutory provider that could integrate community and primary

07:35.840 --> 07:43.360
care services without having to go through a complicated process um of in essence de-merger from an existing ft

07:43.360 --> 07:51.520
uh and without changing the core ft model or freedoms that's a really important point around accountability

07:52.240 --> 07:56.640
uh because we're not here fundamentally trying to change the core accountabilities in the NHS we're

07:56.640 --> 08:03.360
trying to solve particular problems we propose two highly targeted adjustments in relation to the ft regime

08:03.360 --> 08:10.240
and the first is to support mergers or acquisitions of ft's in specified circumstances where this is really

08:10.240 --> 08:17.200
clearly in the patient interest you know for example uh if there's unanimous nhs public stakeholder and

08:17.200 --> 08:24.320
