08:25.520 --> 08:32.320
to avoid nhs trusts being disadvantaged relative to ft's in relation to capital bids

08:32.320 --> 08:40.080
um now this wasn't actually an issue all the while the cdel looked pretty generous but given it's had to

08:40.080 --> 08:46.800
be substantially constrained in recent years in turn it's become necessary for nhs improvement to turn

08:46.800 --> 08:53.360
down what can be strong proposals from nhs trusts for say a and e capital bids simply because there is no

08:53.360 --> 09:01.440
constraint on annual ft capital spend bearing in mind there is an overall national limit and this is patently

09:01.440 --> 09:08.320
unfair for nhs trusts and i just want to emphasize two things here one we are not proposing to change

09:08.320 --> 09:14.480
the wider existing ft freedoms on capital and the intention is that we work very closely with

09:14.480 --> 09:20.720
stakeholders including nhs providers in getting the detail of both of these provisions right we're also

09:20.720 --> 09:29.520
proposing to remove the restriction on local nhs organizations particularly ft's to be able to create

09:30.240 --> 09:37.200
joint decision making committees with other providers and ccgs and i think this proposal we think will

09:37.200 --> 09:47.040
really aid ics governance and as ics is cover the country by 2021 and are typically served by one ccg

09:47.840 --> 09:54.320
we think it would be bar me to create what would be a duplicative and expensive separate statutory vehicle

09:54.320 --> 10:00.320
for icss rather than use this new flexibility around joint committees

10:02.320 --> 10:05.840
it's also worth noting that ccg governing bodies

10:07.280 --> 10:15.200
